ed in any way or to  compare it to something that the doctor  himself or herself might appreciate the  sonic screwdriver and before anyone  asked this is this is from kind of a  snap together you know do-it-yourself  kit there's different pieces you  assemble and then what have you but in  Dave the doctor they have the whole  thing with the war doctor the Tenth  Doctor the eleventh Doctor and they're  all in the cell and they talk about the  sonic screwdriver and how it's the same  device in a different casing that's  effectively what's happened to the  doctor he's the same device and a  different casing that Casey now happens  to be a woman why are we getting hung up  on how that changes the terminology of  the doctors attractions now at this  point I feel like I want to point out  that if I had my way we actually  wouldn't be I would like this to follow  on from what kind of happened with  Capaldi's era which is we're not dealing  with flat-out romantic attractions  anymore there was a little bit like with  him and River Song but and that was a  great deal of affection but if that was  about as close to romantic as he got he  was he was about as close to the more a  sexual doctor that we tended to have in  classic who more often than not so I  would personally like to see that  continue and just not even really have  attractions come up at all but if that's  not going to be the case then I think we  just assign a weird sort of thing to it  we're like oh my god now all of a sudden  the doctors game well no the doctor  hasn't fundamentally changed in in a  sense of what the doctor is attracted to  it's exactly the same so why would you  freak out and go oh god now all of a  sudden he's gay how do I explain that to  my kids but well don't like just if it  cut if by any reason it comes up in the  show at all just say well I mean the  doctor was attracted to him before the  doctor still is so that's how it is and  that's not for me to be trying to  undermine anyone who