pts to deal with the confusions of  just words it's just words so is the  doctor now gay yeah I said yeah  technically but so what the doctor has I  mean what was he alternative well whoa  people who are weirded out by the idea  that the doctor is now gay would you  really rather that the doctor now  expresses an attraction towards a male  character because that means you're  gonna be asking yourself when inevitably  at some point the doctor becomes male  again or even if the doctor stays female  forever you're now going to go back to  those earlier episodes and wonder wait a  minute was the doctor just like being  polite or was he actually into Jack did  the second doctor have a thing with  Jamie like is that what you prefer and  look this is not me saying that the  doctor can't be bisexual or pansexual  much  Jack himself is I think he's perfectly  capable of that we have keep she hi  silly these it depends on which doctor  I'm thinking about at the moment when I  use whatever pronoun I use but you know  that there's been no particularly firm  evidence of any attractions other than  to females so what I have been saying  you know the doctors tried to females  that'll stay the same that's based off  the evidence we have that is not being  exclusionary to all the other  possibilities cuz yeah I don't see any  reason not to and as far as how the  doctor herself would think of herself I  would think that a society in which  people can change their gender from you  know one point their life to another  that seemingly easily and for I  presumably for as long as regeneration  has been a thing one would think that  labels like homosexual an error and a  heterosexual probably either don't exist  or have lost all meaning to a culture  like the Time Lords that's me projecting  a little bit but I mean logically right  I mean if people can just switch back  and forth would you even bother trying  to label that anymore  I don't know so those are just sort of  my thoughts on the